{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02948",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.27,
      "end_seconds": 6.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.73,
      "end_seconds": 12.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.14,
      "end_seconds": 26.73,
      "duration_seconds": 12.59,
      "text": "Well, you know, I've been having fainting on exertion. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.45,
      "end_seconds": 34.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Okay, since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.4,
      "end_seconds": 39.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "It's been two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.41,
      "end_seconds": 43.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.11,
      "end_seconds": 46.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.89,
      "end_seconds": 54.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "So, is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.44,
      "end_seconds": 84.93,
      "duration_seconds": 29.49,
      "text": "Being very breathless goes along with it, most of the time. And there's chest tightness as well, uh, two days now. With chest tightness, about a three out of ten. Oh, uh, the being very breathless? That's been for about four days. Erm, with being very breathless, I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.86,
      "end_seconds": 88.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.34,
      "end_seconds": 93.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.13,
      "end_seconds": 97.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.9,
      "end_seconds": 102.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.64,
      "end_seconds": 105.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.25,
      "end_seconds": 111.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.84,
      "end_seconds": 117.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Okay, any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.26,
      "end_seconds": 130.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "So, you know, my brother has epilepsy. Um, my mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.06,
      "end_seconds": 135.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.44,
      "end_seconds": 149.46,
      "duration_seconds": 12.02,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, you know, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.84,
      "end_seconds": 164.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.66,
      "end_seconds": 169.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.09,
      "end_seconds": 173.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.12,
      "end_seconds": 189.42,
      "duration_seconds": 15.3,
      "text": "Two years now. I'm on alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week for my bones. I do miss it now and then, to be fair. Apixaban I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.22,
      "end_seconds": 193.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Alright, have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.19,
      "end_seconds": 198.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.07,
      "end_seconds": 217.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.77,
      "end_seconds": 235.15,
      "duration_seconds": 15.38,
      "text": "Well, I've had an irregular heartbeat for nearly five years now. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. Yes, heart disease. Thin bones, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.11,
      "end_seconds": 251.18,
      "duration_seconds": 14.07,
      "text": "Right, so an irregular heartbeat and thin bones are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Have you had any leg pain, fever or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.05,
      "end_seconds": 254.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.9,
      "end_seconds": 257.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.36,
      "end_seconds": 260.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.7,
      "end_seconds": 268.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.42,
      "end_seconds": 271.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.01,
      "end_seconds": 292.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.58,
      "end_seconds": 301.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.58,
      "end_seconds": 331.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 138 over 72, temp 36.9 degrees. And heart rate 97, SpO2 90 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.77,
      "end_seconds": 335.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.06,
      "end_seconds": 339.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.89,
      "end_seconds": 345.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.52,
      "end_seconds": 348.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.97,
      "end_seconds": 369.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "There is a loud second heart sound and a raised jugular pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.97,
      "end_seconds": 385.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.59,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Putting it all together, this looks most like possible pulmonary hypertension. I'd also keep a heart valve problem in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.52,
      "end_seconds": 388.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.37,
      "end_seconds": 399.46,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible pulmonary hypertension do well once it's treated properly. Let's get blood tests, for breathlessness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 400.85,
      "end_seconds": 403.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "The earliest is Tuesday, 10 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.23,
      "end_seconds": 405.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.2,
      "end_seconds": 409.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Let's book an echocardiogram to look into exertional syncope."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.79,
      "end_seconds": 413.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.41,
      "end_seconds": 436.56,
      "duration_seconds": 21.15,
      "text": "Let's get an ECG, for syncope. No exertion for now, I am arranging urgent specialist tests. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I'm going to send a referral to the pulmonary hypertension service. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.96,
      "end_seconds": 439.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}